    {'file': 'part-7-multimodal-applications/module-27-multimodal/section-27.4.html', 'svg_idx': 0, 'caption': 'Figure 27.4.1: Pipeline approach (left) chains separate encoders through projection layers, losing information at each handoff. Native multimodal models (right) process all modalities through a single', 'svg_text': 'Pipeline Approach (LLaVA, traditional voice assistants) Vision Encoder (CLIP, frozen) Audio Encoder (Whisper) Text Embedder (tokenizer) Projection ! ! Language Model TTS Model Limitations: Tone and emotion lost during transcription Cumulative latency: 2 to 5 seconds per turn Error propagation with n', 'svg_start': 5077, 'svg_end': 14376},
    {'file': 'part-7-multimodal-applications/module-27-multimodal/section-27.4.html', 'svg_idx': 1, 'caption': 'Figure 27.4.2: Three multimodal fusion strategies. Early fusion (left) allows cross-modal attention at every layer. Late fusion (center) combines separately encoded modalities in a shared decoder. Cro', 'svg_text': 'Early Fusion (GPT-4o, Gemini) Image Audio Text Tokenize + Interleave Layer 1: Full cross-modal attn Layer 2: Full cross-modal attn ... Layer N: Full cross-modal attn cross-modal Any modality output + Deepest cross-modal reasoning - Very expensive to train - Cannot swap individual encoders Late Fusio', 'svg_start': 19898, 'svg_end': 30106},
