    {'file': 'part-8-evaluation-production/module-31-production-engineering/section-31.3.html', 'svg_idx': 0, 'caption': 'Figure 31.3.1: Latency optimization operates at four layers; the highest-impact changes depend on your bottleneck.', 'svg_text': 'Caching Layer: Semantic cache, exact match, KV-cache reuse Request Layer: Batching, request coalescing, priority queues Model Layer: Quantization (GPTQ, AWQ), speculative decoding, distillation Infrastructure Layer: GPU selection, continuous batching (vLLM), tensor parallelism', 'svg_start': 3966, 'svg_end': 5795},
    {'file': 'part-8-evaluation-production/module-31-production-engineering/section-31.3.html', 'svg_idx': 1, 'caption': 'Figure 31.3.2 Complete request flow with rate limiting, backpressure queue, auto-scaling GPU workers, and metrics collection. Rejected requests receive immediate error responses instead of blocking.', 'svg_text': 'Incoming Requests Rate Limiter Token bucket Per-user quotas Burst capacity 429 Too Many Bounded Queue Backpressure signals Priority ordering Health: utilization % 65% 503 Overloaded GPU Worker Pool Auto-scales based on queue depth Worker 1 GPU 0 (active) Worker 2 GPU 1 (active) Worker 3 GPU 2 (activ', 'svg_start': 14170, 'svg_end': 22511},
    {'file': 'part-8-evaluation-production/module-31-production-engineering/section-31.3.html', 'svg_idx': 2, 'caption': 'Figure 31.3.4: Production guardrail pipeline with input rails (pre-generation) and output rails (post-generation) protecting the LLM.', 'svg_text': 'User Input Input Rails Injection, PII, topic control LLM Generation Output Rails Toxicity, facts, hallucination Safe Response Block / Refusal Redact / Retry', 'svg_start': 30074, 'svg_end': 33455},
    {'file': 'part-8-evaluation-production/module-31-production-engineering/section-31.4.html', 'svg_idx': 0, 'caption': 'Figure 31.4.1 The LLMOps lifecycle connects four phases (develop, test, deploy, monitor) through a continuous feedback loop, with a shared registry tracking all artifacts. The code below puts this int', 'svg_text': 'From prompt development through production monitoring to continuous improvement 1. Develop Write prompt template Version with hash Offline eval (test set) Choose model + params 2. A/B Test Hash-based splitting Run both variants Collect online metrics Statistical evaluation 3. Deploy Promote winner M', 'svg_start': 5256, 'svg_end': 13287},
